                                <p>The original 5.56x45mm round was designed in the United States and is known as the M193 family. This round was used in the early version of the M16 assault rifle and various other weapons. Compared to the improved NATO round it has a lighter bullet, uses a more fouling propellant, has a higher muzzle velocity and uses a longer rifling twist rate. Ammunition of the M193 pattern is or was produced in many nations.</p>
